# SAEA-BENCH-slicebatch — step-2 equivalence + throughput bench (owner
# directive 2026-08-12 "直接进入step2").
#
# obs_batch_slices=4 on the fixed-window/no-tail substrate: every window cut
# and registered before the first model touch, then dispatched through a
# 4-worker pool over the SAME retry/saturation seam; acceptance, traces and
# stitch chains emitted in slice order. Legality (fixed + tail=0 + trim=0)
# enforced fail-closed in ObsLoopConfig.from_values.
#
# Reference: the sequential notail run fac835 (19 min / WER 0.1409, same
# split, same per-slice prompts — only scheduling differs).
# Runs TWICE under this row. Pre-registered readings:
#   (i)  WER within the notail run's vicinity (prompts byte-identical);
#   (ii) wall < 19 min (straggler elimination: loop effective concurrency
#        was ~2.6/4, slice dispatch keeps 4/4 busy);
#   (iii) run-2 vs run-1 byte-compare — determinism under slice dispatch
#        (zero cross-slice dependencies; thinker batch noise isolated);
#   (iv) concurrency decoupled from sample count by construction (3 samples
#        cannot saturate 4 slots at sample level; slice level can).
# Adoption: (i)+(ii) hold -> slice-parallel becomes the default bare-core
# substrate for new arms alongside the S1/notail re-registration.
#
# run_id:baseline_fragment
SAEA-BENCH-slicebatch:fixed-batch-bare
